  "preamble": "Fortition of the retroflex approximant [ɻ] to the voiced retroflex stop [ɖ]. Early Telugu still had the Proto-Dravidian approximant *ɻ (ḻ), but it later merged with /ɖ/, so Telugu has ḍ where Tamil keeps ḻ: Proto-South Dravidian *kōẓi 'chicken' > Telugu kōḍi, Tamil kōḻi.",
